<tool id="argnorm" name="argNorm" version="1.0.0+galaxy0" profile="21.05">
  <description>Normalize ARG annotations to the ARO</description>
  <macros />
  <xrefs>
    <xref type="bio.tools">argnorm</xref>
  </xrefs>
  <requirements>
    <requirement type="package" version="1.0.0">argnorm</requirement>
  </requirements>
  <command detect_errors="exit_code">
        argnorm
        --input '$input'
        --output '$output'
        --threads \${GALAXY_SLOTS:-1}
        --log '$log'
        --version
    </command>
  <inputs>
    <param name="input" type="data" format="tabular" label="Input file" help="Input file must be a tabular file with headers" />
  </inputs>
  <outputs>
    <data name="output" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Normalized ARGs" />
    <data name="log" format="txt" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Log file" />
  </outputs>
  <tests>
    <test>
      <param name="input" value="argnorm_input.tsv" />
      <output name="output" file="argnorm_output.tsv" ftype="tabular" lines_diff="2" />
      <output name="log" file="argnorm_log.txt" ftype="txt" lines_diff="2" />
    </test>
  </tests>
  <help>
        argNorm is a tool to normalize antibiotic resistance genes (ARGs) by mapping them to the antibiotic resistance ontology (ARO) created by the CARD database.

        argNorm also enhances antibiotic resistance gene annotations by providing drug categorization of the drugs that antibiotic resistance genes confer resistance to.
    </help>
  <citations>
    <citation type="doi">10.1093/bioinformatics/btab108</citation>
    <citation type="bibtex">@misc{galaxy_toolsmith,
  title = {Galaxy Toolsmith},
  howpublished = {\url{https://github.com/BlankenbergLab/galaxy-toolsmith}},
  url = {https://github.com/BlankenbergLab/galaxy-toolsmith}
}</citation>
  </citations>
</tool>